      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 mb-6">
        The Von Neumann digital architecture partitions computation into three synchronized domains: the Central Processing Unit (CPU), the Storage/Memory Unit, and the Input/Output (I/O) Subsystem. Communication between these elements occurs through three specialized bus structures: the <strong>Data Bus</strong> (bidirectional data payload), the <strong>Control Bus</strong> (synchronizing command signals), and the <strong>Address Bus</strong> (memory mapping).
      </p>

