            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-sky-600"></span> 1. Fetch Cycle &amp; Address Bus
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            The <strong>Program Counter (PC)</strong> places the address of the subsequent instruction onto the unidirectional <em>Address Bus</em> directed to the Memory Address Register (MAR). The Control Unit asserts a <code>MEM_READ</code> signal, retrieving the machine opcode via the bidirectional <em>Data Bus</em> into the Instruction Register (IR).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-slate-50/50">
          <div class="text-indigo-700 font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 flex items-center gap-1.5">
