          </div>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            The <strong>Instruction Decoder</strong> in the CU analyzes the opcode and addressing modes. It generates synchronized microcode pulses across the <em>Control Bus</em> to regulate clock gating, register multiplexers, and ALU operation modes while fetching required operands from RAM.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-slate-50/50">
          <div class="text-emerald-700 font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-600"></span> 3. Execute &amp; I/O Handshake
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            The <strong>ALU</strong> computes mathematical or bitwise logic, loading results into the Accumulator. When communicating with peripherals, memory-mapped I/O or DMA (Direct Memory Access) controllers handle high-bandwidth transfers to output framebuffers without stalling the main processor core.
          </p>
